{{- /*
  blog/blog-config-fragment — inline ONE user-config fragment of the blog
  suite AT RENDER TIME.

  Config files live under `{{ Arg "Folder" "blog/posts" }}/.mitto/<Name>.md`,
  one topic per file. Standard fragments: audience, tone, topics, frontmatter,
  publish-checklist, linkedin-template.

  Architectural intent (mitto-98l.1): the fragment CONTENT is embedded verbatim
  into the rendered prompt via Go text/template — the agent never reads the
  file at runtime. This makes prompts auditable (the exact bytes the agent
  received are visible in event logs), deterministic (no per-run filesystem
  drift), and cheaper (no shell/tool round-trip). Mirrors
  support/shared/channel-fragment-read.

  When the fragment file is MISSING, the template falls back to the caller-
  supplied `DefaultText` verbatim (no BEGIN/END markers around the default —
  callers get exactly the bytes they asked for).

  Callers pass named fields via a `dict`:

      Name:        short filename stem (no extension). One of:
                   "audience" | "tone" | "topics" | "frontmatter"
                   | "publish-checklist" | "linkedin-template".
                   Required.
      DefaultText: fallback body to emit verbatim when the file is missing.
                   May be empty (the fragment then emits nothing on miss).

  Usage (rendered as a Markdown block — the CALLER supplies any leading
  bullet/heading):

      {{ template "blog/shared/blog-config-fragment"
           (dict "Name"        "audience"
                 "DefaultText" "Expert practitioners, slightly informal, direct, no hand-holding.") }}
*/ -}}
{{- $name := .Name -}}
{{- $default := .DefaultText -}}
{{- $folder := Arg "Folder" "blog/posts" -}}
{{- $path := printf "%s/.mitto/%s.md" $folder $name -}}
{{- if FileExists $path -}}
**Blog `{{ $name }}` (embedded from `{{ $path }}`)** — this is the authoritative
`{{ $name }}` guide for this blog. It **overrides** the generic default below.

<!-- BEGIN {{ $path }} -->
{{ ReadFile $path }}
<!-- END {{ $path }} -->
{{- else -}}
{{ $default }}
{{- end -}}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
